WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.080 --> 00:00:03.788
Welcome to Hearthhold!

2
00:00:03.788 --> 00:00:09.756
In this video you will learn how to play by watching a real game against the computer, step by step.

3
00:00:10.960 --> 00:00:15.420
Two villages grow side by side for three years, one round per season.

4
00:00:15.420 --> 00:00:19.731
You build, take in travellers, and keep everyone fed, housed and warm.

5
00:00:19.731 --> 00:00:22.548
Every night a creature attacks both villages.

6
00:00:22.548 --> 00:00:26.212
After twelve rounds, the village with the most points wins.

7
00:00:29.200 --> 00:00:30.844
This is the home page.

8
00:00:30.844 --> 00:00:35.361
The Game lobby button at the top left takes you back to all the board games.

9
00:00:36.320 --> 00:00:41.399
First pick your opponent: the computer, a friend on the same device, or Online,

10
00:00:41.399 --> 00:00:46.428
where you challenge another Ahrens Labs player and each take your turn whenever you like.

11
00:00:47.920 --> 00:00:52.508
Choose how strong the computer is, name your village, and pick who goes first.

12
00:00:52.508 --> 00:00:54.039
We will go first.

13
00:01:00.200 --> 00:01:04.653
Across the top you can see the twelve seasons. We are in Spring of year one.

14
00:01:05.440 --> 00:01:09.025
Below that are the threats: tonight’s creature and the next two.

15
00:01:09.025 --> 00:01:12.803
Tonight a Wolf pack, strength three, attacks our south-west side.

16
00:01:12.803 --> 00:01:16.723
Our defense is only one, so right now we would lose three food.

17
00:01:18.360 --> 00:01:20.025
These are the locations.

18
00:01:20.025 --> 00:01:24.912
Each game uses five, drawn from twenty, so every game is a little different.

19
00:01:24.912 --> 00:01:29.685
Each one holds just one worker per round, so whoever gets there first takes it.

20
00:01:31.360 --> 00:01:36.332
Below them are two always-open places, the Village commons and Odd jobs.

21
00:01:36.332 --> 00:01:42.044
They give much less, but any number of workers can go there, so a spare worker is never wasted.

22
00:01:43.640 --> 00:01:46.948
This is your village: nineteen hexes around your Keep.

23
00:01:46.948 --> 00:01:53.819
Meadows take farms or town buildings, forests take lumber camps, hills take quarries and mountains take mines.

24
00:01:53.819 --> 00:01:56.693
You start with a Keep, a Farm and two Peasants.

25
00:01:58.600 --> 00:02:02.889
Your stores are on the right: food, wood, stone, iron and gold.

26
00:02:02.889 --> 00:02:07.605
The panel also warns you if supper or tonight’s fight is going to go badly.

27
00:02:07.605 --> 00:02:10.224
Scores stay secret until the very end.

28
00:02:11.960 --> 00:02:13.860
Each round you get two workers.

29
00:02:13.860 --> 00:02:19.472
On your turn you send one worker to an empty location and get its reward right away.

30
00:02:19.472 --> 00:02:24.651
That ends your turn. Let’s send one to the Builders’ yard for two wood and two stone.

31
00:02:27.120 --> 00:02:30.833
Now the computer takes its turn, and it places a worker too.

32
00:02:30.833 --> 00:02:34.796
Watch the locations and the chronicle at the bottom of the page.

33
00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:40.923
The computer went to the Mill fields. That spot is now blocked for us this round.

34
00:02:41.680 --> 00:02:46.545
Besides workers, you have free actions. You can do as many as you can pay for,

35
00:02:46.545 --> 00:02:52.065
before or after placing a worker: build, put up walls, recruit travellers and trade.

36
00:02:53.600 --> 00:02:58.913
First, the wolves. A Palisade costs two wood and adds two defense on one side.

37
00:02:58.913 --> 00:03:03.089
On the south-west side, that makes three, and we drive the wolves off.

38
00:03:04.520 --> 00:03:09.599
Next, more food. Click Build to see every building, what it costs and what it does.

39
00:03:09.599 --> 00:03:11.748
A Farm costs just one wood.

40
00:03:13.040 --> 00:03:18.048
Pick it, then choose a glowing meadow. Farms next to a Well make one more food.

41
00:03:18.800 --> 00:03:22.684
Down here is the Crossroads, where travellers wait for a new home.

42
00:03:22.684 --> 00:03:25.672
The first in line is cheapest but leaves tonight.

43
00:03:25.672 --> 00:03:30.680
This Farmer costs only one gold, and makes more food than a Peasant on a Farm.

44
00:03:32.400 --> 00:03:35.025
Every villager needs a bed and water.

45
00:03:35.025 --> 00:03:38.248
We have room for one more, so let’s take the Farmer in.

46
00:03:38.248 --> 00:03:41.357
New villagers get to work on a Farm right away.

47
00:03:42.720 --> 00:03:44.087
Short of something?

48
00:03:44.087 --> 00:03:49.037
Trading is free too: two of anything for one of anything else, as often as you like.

49
00:03:49.037 --> 00:03:52.403
A Merchant, or the Trading post, makes it one for one.

50
00:03:54.560 --> 00:03:57.697
Now our second worker. We’ll take the Militia yard.

51
00:03:57.697 --> 00:04:04.305
Because it is our last worker, our turn doesn’t end: we can still use free actions, and then press End round.

52
00:04:05.760 --> 00:04:11.195
When you are done, press End round. Any worker you didn’t place is lost, so use them both!

53
00:04:14.560 --> 00:04:17.719
Once both villages have ended the round, night falls.

54
00:04:17.719 --> 00:04:22.584
First every worked building produces. Then the creature attacks both villages.

55
00:04:22.584 --> 00:04:28.296
With the palisade and the militia our defense held, so we win the wolves’ trophy, worth one point.

56
00:04:30.400 --> 00:04:33.303
Then supper: every villager eats one food.

57
00:04:33.303 --> 00:04:36.461
If you are short, villagers leave and you lose points.

58
00:04:36.461 --> 00:04:41.000
In Winter, farms rest and every three villagers also burn one wood.

59
00:04:42.640 --> 00:04:46.837
Finally the front traveller leaves the Crossroads, and new ones arrive.

60
00:04:52.480 --> 00:04:57.068
In Summer the computer goes first, because the first player switches every round.

61
00:04:57.068 --> 00:04:59.181
Next come two flying creatures.

62
00:04:59.181 --> 00:05:04.445
Walls don’t stop flyers, so you will need Archers, a Watchtower or the Militia yard.

63
00:05:06.200 --> 00:05:08.207
Now let’s go through every rule.

64
00:05:08.207 --> 00:05:12.688
The rules are always one click away, from the Rules button in the top bar.

65
00:05:12.688 --> 00:05:16.608
The first tab is this video, so you can come back to it any time.

66
00:05:18.200 --> 00:05:20.057
Each round has three parts.

67
00:05:20.057 --> 00:05:25.584
In the morning each village gets its workers: two, or three once a Steward works your Keep.

68
00:05:25.584 --> 00:05:30.293
In the day you take turns. At dusk the night plays out for both villages.

69
00:05:32.080 --> 00:05:37.607
On your turn you can do any number of free actions, then place one worker, or press End round.

70
00:05:37.607 --> 00:05:42.636
Once you end the round you are done until tomorrow, and unplaced workers are wasted.

71
00:05:44.200 --> 00:05:47.231
Anything a place gives you for tonight or this round,

72
00:05:47.231 --> 00:05:50.539
like the Militia yard’s defense or the Tavern’s discount,

73
00:05:50.539 --> 00:05:52.795
wears off when the next round starts.

74
00:05:54.080 --> 00:05:59.564
The seasons matter. In Summer worked farms make one more food, and in Autumn two more.

75
00:05:59.564 --> 00:06:04.892
In Winter farms make nothing, and every three villagers burn one wood to stay warm.

76
00:06:06.600 --> 00:06:12.340
Workers and places lists all twenty main places in five groups: food, materials,

77
00:06:12.340 --> 00:06:15.435
coin and trade, people and renown, and defense.

78
00:06:15.435 --> 00:06:19.077
Each game uses one from every group, marked with a tick.

79
00:06:20.840 --> 00:06:24.617
Each main place holds one worker per round, from either village.

80
00:06:24.617 --> 00:06:27.449
You get the reward the moment you place the worker.

81
00:06:28.480 --> 00:06:33.665
At the bottom are the two always-open places, the Village commons and Odd jobs.

82
00:06:33.665 --> 00:06:39.889
They give just one food or one gold, but there is no limit, even for several of your own workers.

83
00:06:41.600 --> 00:06:44.417
The fine print covers every special case,

84
00:06:44.417 --> 00:06:47.363
like the Moneylender taking your points below zero,

85
00:06:47.363 --> 00:06:50.835
or the Mason’s lodge never building higher than stone.

86
00:06:52.240 --> 00:06:54.311
Free actions need no worker.

87
00:06:54.311 --> 00:06:58.792
Build as many buildings as you can pay for, on a free hex of the right land.

88
00:06:58.792 --> 00:07:03.977
Walls defend only their own side: a palisade costs two wood for two defense,

89
00:07:03.977 --> 00:07:07.065
and stone costs three stone more for four in total.

90
00:07:09.160 --> 00:07:12.297
You can also trade two of anything for one of anything else,

91
00:07:12.297 --> 00:07:15.684
and move villagers between jobs at any time on your turn.

92
00:07:16.760 --> 00:07:22.927
At the Crossroads, the first traveller costs two gold less, and the second one less, but never below one.

93
00:07:22.927 --> 00:07:25.040
Taking someone moves the line up.

94
00:07:25.040 --> 00:07:28.881
It only refills at night, when the front traveller leaves for good.

95
00:07:28.881 --> 00:07:31.777
A Peasant for one gold is always available.

96
00:07:33.960 --> 00:07:37.652
Each traveller has a trade and works best in their own building.

97
00:07:37.652 --> 00:07:41.173
Anyone can work a farm, lumber camp, quarry or mine.

98
00:07:41.173 --> 00:07:45.157
Each building holds one worker, except the Barracks, which holds two.

99
00:07:46.760 --> 00:07:51.583
At night, in order: buildings work, Blacksmiths forge arms, the creature attacks,

100
00:07:51.583 --> 00:07:56.789
everyone eats supper, in Winter you burn firewood, and then the Crossroads changes.

101
00:07:56.789 --> 00:08:01.328
For every food or wood you are short, a villager leaves and you lose a point.

102
00:08:03.480 --> 00:08:08.367
Your defense adds up: one from the Keep, one per set of arms, your Guards, Knights,

103
00:08:08.367 --> 00:08:11.781
Archers and Wizard, the wall on the side being attacked,

104
00:08:11.781 --> 00:08:15.808
and anything tonight’s places gave you. Flyers ignore walls.

105
00:08:17.640 --> 00:08:22.463
If your defense is at least the creature’s strength, you drive it off and win its trophy.

106
00:08:22.463 --> 00:08:27.008
If not, it might take resources, knock down a wall, carry off a villager,

107
00:08:27.008 --> 00:08:31.675
turn one to stone, or burn a building. This table explains each one.

108
00:08:33.680 --> 00:08:38.289
The Buildings tab shows every building, its cost, its land and its points.

109
00:08:38.289 --> 00:08:41.640
Buildings with a job only score while someone works there.

110
00:08:41.640 --> 00:08:45.795
Houses sleep three, and Wells give water for four more villagers.

111
00:08:47.560 --> 00:08:52.255
Three buildings are wonders: the Castle, the Wizard’s Tower and the Cathedral.

112
00:08:52.255 --> 00:08:57.049
Only one village can build each, and you need five or seven villagers first.

113
00:08:58.520 --> 00:09:03.513
The Villagers tab shows all seventeen kinds of traveller: their price, what they do,

114
00:09:03.513 --> 00:09:08.393
where they work and their points. A Steward gives you an extra worker every round.

115
00:09:09.880 --> 00:09:14.319
Round one is always the Wolf pack. Creatures get stronger every year:

116
00:09:14.319 --> 00:09:18.011
strength three or four in year one, seven to nine in year two,

117
00:09:18.011 --> 00:09:20.437
and thirteen or fourteen in year three.

118
00:09:21.960 --> 00:09:26.889
Creatures on foot attack one side, shown on the map. Flyers come over the walls.

119
00:09:26.889 --> 00:09:31.705
Each card shows the trophy for driving it off, and the damage if it breaks through.

120
00:09:33.200 --> 00:09:38.343
At the end, points come from renown, staffed buildings, villagers, one per stone wall,

121
00:09:38.343 --> 00:09:42.739
three for walls on all six sides, and one per five leftover gold.

122
00:09:42.739 --> 00:09:45.933
On a tie, the village with more villagers wins.

123
00:09:47.760 --> 00:09:51.275
And at the bottom are some strategy tips to get you started.

124
00:09:52.480 --> 00:09:54.849
Let’s skip ahead to the end of year three.

125
00:09:54.849 --> 00:10:00.305
Scores stay hidden all game, so the end is a big reveal, one category at a time.

126
00:10:07.440 --> 00:10:12.284
Each category is added up for both villages, and the winner is crowned at the end.

127
00:10:12.284 --> 00:10:16.012
From here you can start a new game, or go back to the lobby.

128
00:10:18.120 --> 00:10:23.412
Remember: watch tonight’s threat, keep food for Winter, and use every worker each round.

129
00:10:23.412 --> 00:10:27.083
Your game saves in your browser, so you can come back any time.

130
00:10:27.083 --> 00:10:30.817
To play a friend online, pick Online when you start a new game.

131
00:10:30.817 --> 00:10:33.479
Good luck, and have fun building your village!

